          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Statement"} Statement
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Thom-Gysin sequence
            is a type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+in+cohomology"} long exact sequence in cohomology
            induced by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibration"} spherical fibration
            and expressing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
            of the total space in terms of those of the base plus correction. The sequence may be obtained as a corollary of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre spectral sequence
            for the given fibration. It induces, and is induced by, the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
          %h2#Statement Statement
          #ThomGysinSequence.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi π
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^n &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; E
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; B
                    }
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              with typical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#FibersOfSerreFibrations"}> exmpl.
              ) the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            %p
              Then there exists an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ;
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in H^{n+1}(B; R)
              (in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
              of the total space with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+class"} Euler class
              of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
              operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \cup (-)
              sits in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ;
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi π
                          %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ;
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ;
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ;
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    H^k(B; R)
                    \\stackrel{\pi^\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    H^k(E; R)
                    \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                    H^{k-n}(B;R)
                    \\stackrel{c \cup (-)}{\longrightarrow}
                    H^{k+1}(B; R)
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Switzer75"} Switzer 75, section 15.30
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Kochmann96"} Kochman 96, corollary 2.2.6
          #ProofOfThomGysinSequence.proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Under the given assumptions there is the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre spectral sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
